id,title,total,days,first,last,corrective,shape,guard
編號,標題,總次數,發生天數,首次,最近,矯正措施,形狀,守衛
1,"Stopped part-way through an agreed queue and reported instead of continuing",3,2,2026-09-08,2026-09-09,"Scripts/queue_heartbeat.zsh plus a /loop that reads it: the next item is named by a file, not by memory","A unit of work finishes, the report is written, and the turn ends -- with items still on the list the user had asked to be worked through. Nothing fails; the report is accurate about what was done and silent about what was not started","Scripts/queue_heartbeat.zsh (prints the next unchecked item, or IDLE when the switch is off)"
2,A new source file is not picked up by an incremental build,1,1,2026-09-10,2026-09-10,Delete .build/release.yaml before the first build after adding a file; touch Package.swift does NOT work because SwiftPM hashes manifest content,"A file is added to a target directory, the compile phase is completely clean, and the LINKER reports undefined symbol: <the new function>. That reads as a missing library or a bad declaration, not as a file that was never compiled. release.yaml was three hours stale and still listed the old source set","git diff --stat after a regenerate, and: ls -l .build/release.yaml -- if it predates the new file, the plan cannot know about it"
3,Added a way to change the target window and left the identity half undone,3,2,2026-09-09,2026-09-10,"When adding an action that RETARGETS anything, treat currentWindowIdentity() as a required second half, not an optional extra: grep every Synthesiser for the override before calling the action done. Three platforms, three spellings, one silent failure","focus succeeds, the replay reports every action completed, and every later coordinate still resolves against the window measured before the replay began. Nothing errors -- each coordinate is a real number, just relative to the wrong window","grep -c currentWindowIdentity across all Synthesiser files; a synthesiser with 0 returns the protocol default of 0, and 0 is exactly what replay reads as cannot-tell"
4,Ran a tool against a filename that does not exist and read no output as a clean result,3,1,2026-09-10,2026-09-10,"Any conclusion whose CONTENT is a zero needs a positive control run by the SAME command -- something known to match. For a path, put ls -l on the expected OUTPUT in the same command; on the third occurrence that is what contradicted the zero within a second","A tool prints nothing and the nothing looks exactly like good news: objdump on libgtk-4-1.dll (real name gtk-4-1.dll) read as zero symbols; grep -cE for errors after zsh compile.sh (real name compile.zsh) read as a clean build; and compile.zsh -winui, a flag that does not exist, printed Missing source file which is not a compiler diagnostic and so scored 0 errors too","ls -l every path before handing it to a tool AND ls -l the expected output after; before writing down a zero, name what would make that command print non-zero, then make it print once"
5,"Read a dead process as a slow one, and invented a mechanism to explain it",1,1,2026-09-10,2026-09-10,"Before explaining WHY something is slow, check that it is still running: pgrep the process, or diff against the last version that worked (git stash / git checkout -- the file). An explanation must come after the process is confirmed alive, never before.","P52 gained a fourth arm; four per-arm arrays were still count:3, so lastSentinel[3] terminated the process before step one. The log ended after CONFIG with no crash message and no non-zero exit anywhere I looked, which reads exactly like a benchmark that has stalled. I attributed it to AppKit throttling redraws in a background window -- a real mechanism, which is what made it convincing -- and re-ran it in the foreground to test that. Reverting the file to HEAD took one command and answered it: the original completed, so I had broken it.","git checkout -- <file> and re-run BEFORE theorising, whenever the thing that changed is mine. It is one command and it separates my defect from the platform."
6,"Reported a test suite as passing from a grep of its output, without its exit code",1,1,2026-09-10,2026-09-10,"Read the runner verdict, not a filter of the log. run_checked.zsh exists for exactly this and prints an exit status; `grep -aE ... | tail` does not. When a summary line is wanted AND the verdict, capture the run to a file, echo $? on its own line, then grep the file.","A rename removed LazyVGrid.resolve and plan.columnWidths, which GridLayoutTests still used, so SwiftCrossUITests could not BUILD. Scripts/test.sh runs more than one test invocation; a later one built and printed `Test run with 68 tests ... passed`, and my grep for `Test run with|✗` matched that line and nothing else. The compile error had the word `error:` and no checkmark, so it fell outside the pattern. I committed with the message `Scripts/test.sh passes`, which was false, and only found it an hour later when the same filter finally showed the error on an unrelated run.",Never let the pattern decide the verdict. Run through run_checked.zsh and read its exit status on its own line before writing any claim about a build or a test run.
